<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/4th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Campaign</p><h1 class="enc-title">Aksumite conquest of Kush</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 350 CE</span> · <a href="/centuries/4th-century">4th century</a> · Also known as Ezana's conquest of the Kingdom of Kush</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Aksumite conquest of Kush was the campaign led by the Aksumite king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ezana">Ezana</a> around 350 CE against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kushite-empire">Kingdom of Kush</a> and its centre at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/meroe">Meroë</a>. Ezana recorded the expedition in an inscription. It showed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aksumite-empire">Aksum</a>'s military reach into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nile">Nile</a> valley and coincided with the final decline of Kush.</p></div>
